    "icon": "data:image/png;base64,",
    "description": "Draws a reproducible random sample within strata: proportional with a minimum per stratum, equal, fixed number or percentage, with sampling weights and an allocation table.",
    "category": "Preparation",
    "subcategory": "Sampling",
    "tags": [
        "sample",
        "stratified",
        "audit sampling",
        "random",
        "split",
        "survey",
        "visokio-agents"
    ],
    "introductoryText": "Draws a random sample in which **every group (stratum) is represented**: regions, risk bands, customer segments, store formats. A simple random sample can miss small groups entirely; a stratified one cannot.\n\n- **Proportional**: a total sample size split across strata in proportion to their size, with a **minimum per stratum** so small groups still get a few records (largest-remainder rounding, never more than a stratum holds)\n- **Equal**: a total sample size split equally across strata\n- **Fixed number per stratum**: for example 10 from each\n- **Percentage per stratum**: for example 5% of each\n\nSampling is without replacement and **reproducible**: the same seed gives the same sample. Each sampled record gets a **Sample Weight** (stratum population / stratum sample size) for estimating population totals, and its stratum label. The **remainder** output holds the records not sampled (for train / test splits or control groups), and the **allocation** output shows population, sample size, fraction and weight per stratum.",
    "dependencies": "",
